WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.988 --> 00:00:14.870
next weekend my friends and I climbed aboard a big luxury bus.

2
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.571
We were headed for our mountain getaway with Mr.

3
00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:20.672
Chen. Bunch came too, of course.

4
00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:23.773
But he had to travel in his dog cage.

5
00:00:24.674 --> 00:00:26.014
We found seats on the bus.

6
00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:29.996
All around us, lots of people were talking and laughing.

7
00:00:31.184 --> 00:00:34.626
I guess we weren't the only ones excited about a mountain getaway!

8
00:00:35.506 --> 00:00:37.387
Caswell was sitting next to Molly.

9
00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:40.768
He had his huge teddy bear backpack with him.

10
00:00:40.788 --> 00:00:43.109
"Are we there yet?"

11
00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.109
he asked her.

12
00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:50.652
"Caswell, the bus hasn't even left yet," said Molly, laughing at her little brother.

13
00:00:50.672 --> 00:00:54.834
"So how could we be there already?"

14
00:00:56.074 --> 00:00:59.616
The bus finally pulled out of the station a few minutes later.

15
00:01:00.624 --> 00:01:03.567
I smiled to myself and patted my backpack.

16
00:01:04.507 --> 00:01:08.851
Besides my clothes, the backpack contained my secret invention.

17
00:01:10.412 --> 00:01:13.815
From inside his dog cage, Bunch kept sniffing the air.

18
00:01:15.316 --> 00:01:19.319
He could probably smell the hamster pellets I had used for my invention.

19
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.502
Bunch loves hamster pellets.

20
00:01:23.342 --> 00:01:24.623
He was even drooling!

21
00:01:25.844 --> 00:01:29.848
Mr. Chen had brought a big suitcase that held his magic tricks.

22
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.381
When he wasn't working at the supermarket, Mr.

23
00:01:33.461 --> 00:01:35.882
Chen sometimes performed magic shows.

24
00:01:36.882 --> 00:01:40.704
Once I'd seen him make a frog leap out of his shirt sleeve.

25
00:01:41.504 --> 00:01:43.585
The audience had loved that trick.

26
00:01:44.826 --> 00:01:46.766
Molly had noticed the suitcase too.

27
00:01:46.786 --> 00:01:50.528
"Mr. Chen, can we see your magic things?"

28
00:01:51.088 --> 00:01:51.668
she asked.

29
00:01:51.688 --> 00:01:54.009
"Sure," said Mr.

30
00:01:54.089 --> 00:01:55.190
Chen with a smile.

31
00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.751
"I'm working on some new tricks.

32
00:01:58.271 --> 00:02:00.532
I'm going to practice them at Shadow Lake Lodge."

33
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.482
He took his suitcase down from the overhead rack.

34
00:02:05.622 --> 00:02:11.466
He showed us some of the things inside: gold coins, playing cards, and a magic wand.

35
00:02:11.486 --> 00:02:14.368
"Are we there yet?"

36
00:02:14.628 --> 00:02:16.309
Caswell kept asking.

37
00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:19.131
Molly covered her face with her hands.

38
00:02:20.051 --> 00:02:22.133
But Josh smiled patiently.

39
00:02:22.153 --> 00:02:25.174
"Not yet, Caswell," he said.

40
00:02:25.194 --> 00:02:27.496
"But we're going into a cool tunnel now!"

41
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.422
"This tunnel goes under a river," I added.

42
00:02:36.824 --> 00:02:39.085
Caswell peered nervously through the window.

43
00:02:39.105 --> 00:02:45.050
"I hope the river doesn't fall on our heads," he said.

44
00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:48.533
"Don't worry, Caswell," said Mr.

45
00:02:48.613 --> 00:02:50.995
Chen. "This tunnel is strong.

46
00:02:51.395 --> 00:02:52.496
It will keep the river out."

47
00:02:53.817 --> 00:02:57.140
When we came out of the tunnel, we were not in the city anymore.

48
00:03:00.242 --> 00:03:01.904
We were on a busy highway.

49
00:03:02.844 --> 00:03:06.367
In the distance I could see hills with colorful fall trees.

50
00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:12.332
An hour later the bus was climbing a steep mountain road.

51
00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.575
It led up to Shadow Lake Lodge.

52
00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:23.521
my gosh!"

53
00:03:24.022 --> 00:03:24.862
Jenny gasped.

54
00:03:24.882 --> 00:03:27.605
"This is where we're staying?"

55
00:03:28.045 --> 00:03:28.765
said Josh.

56
00:03:28.786 --> 00:03:32.733
"Caswell, guess what," Molly whispered.

57
00:03:32.753 --> 00:03:34.735
"We're finally here."

58
00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.839
I was staring at the building in amazement too.

59
00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.763
I decided that Shadow Lake Lodge wasn't really a hotel.

60
00:03:46.504 --> 00:03:49.407
It was a fairy-tale castle sitting on a mountain.

61
00:03:50.588 --> 00:03:52.590
Flags flew from its towers.

62
00:03:54.131 --> 00:03:55.612
Hills rippled below.

63
00:03:57.193 --> 00:03:59.936
A blue lake glittered in the sunlight.

64
00:04:02.092 --> 00:04:03.753
"I can't wait to see our room!"

65
00:04:04.173 --> 00:04:04.834
said Molly.

66
00:04:04.854 --> 00:04:07.775
"Maybe it will have gold curtains."

67
00:04:07.795 --> 00:04:12.558
"And diamond tables," said Jenny.

68
00:04:13.739 --> 00:04:14.559
Molly giggled.

69
00:04:14.579 --> 00:04:17.421
"We'll be like princesses!"

70
00:04:17.441 --> 00:04:22.844
"Maybe we'll be invited to a fancy ball tonight," said Jenny.

71
00:04:25.746 --> 00:04:26.706
Josh gave me a look.

72
00:04:27.307 --> 00:04:28.107
The look meant, "Ugh!

73
00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:32.457
Girls." I knew just how he felt.

74
00:04:33.257 --> 00:04:36.559
I didn't care about gold curtains or diamond tables either.

75
00:04:37.559 --> 00:04:40.040
And I definitely didn't care about fancy balls.

76
00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:45.042
"I want to hike up to that lookout tower," I said.

77
00:04:45.062 --> 00:04:49.964
I pointed to a tall stone tower at the very top of the mountain.

78
00:04:49.984 --> 00:04:52.826
"Me too!"

79
00:04:53.266 --> 00:04:54.026
cried Josh.

80
00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.908
I had never climbed a mountain before.

81
00:04:59.336 --> 00:05:04.366
I patted my backpack again, really glad that I had brought along my latest invention.

82
00:05:05.669 --> 00:05:11.019
Looking up at the steep mountain, I had a feeling that we were going to need my invention.
